<title>JAPAN: Eisai, Janssen agree to jointly market ulcer drug.</title>
<headline>Eisai, Janssen agree to jointly market ulcer drug.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Eisai Co Ltd said on Tuesday it had agreed with Janssen Pharmaceutica NV, a Belgian unit of Johnson &amp; Johnson of the United States, to jointly market Eisai's ulcer drug rabeprazole.</p>
<p>Under the agreement, Eisai and Janssen will cooperate in marketing rabeprazole in the United States, Britain, Germany and France. Janssen will have exclusive rights to market the drug in areas excluding those four countries and excluding Asia, Italy, Spain, Belgium and the Netherlands.</p>
<p>The drug, sold under the trademark Pariet, is currently under review for marketing approval by the Japanese Ministry of Health and Welfare and by the Medicines Control Agency in Britain, Eisai said in a statement.</p>
<p>The drug is currently going through the last phase of three-stage clinical trials in the United States, the statement said.</p>
</text>
